	(text "PD_IRQ (PB4/EXTI4), active low.\nR30 provides the 3.3 V pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 115.57 59.182 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c3a863d4-9fb4-4ca8-a540-6f72442c1734")
	)
	(text "RESET / ROM BOOT STATES\nAfter reset, GPIOs begin as high-impedance analog inputs; the board pull resistors establish the initial levels.\nDefaults: PB4/p24 PD_IRQ high (R30 10k); PB3/p23 PD_ENABLE low/off (R10 100k); PC15/p2 USER_BUTTON_N high (R31 100k);\nPA15/p22 PD_PGOOD high (R11 10k); PB5/p25 INA_ALERT high (R19 10k); PB8/p28 BUCK_PGOOD high (R16 10k). PA0/p6 LED_DATA_RAW remains high impedance until firmware configures it.\nIn system ROM, PB0/p14 is FDCAN RX (pull-up) and PB1/p15 is FDCAN TX (push-pull, pull-up).\nPA4/p10, PA5/p11, and PA7/p13 become internally pulled-down SPI inputs; PA6/p12 becomes the SPI MISO push-pull output. These four pins are intentionally unconnected.\nPC15/p2, PA0/p6, PA15/p22, PB3/p23, PB4/p24, PB5/p25, and PB8/p28 are not claimed by the ROM bootloader, so their board-defined states remain."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e4166192-0048-48a1-a183-01d45bf761b7")
	)
